       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is double the maximum recommended dose. It adds no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit over 3,200 mg/day and substantially raises the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm. I don't see a clinical scenario where this is a safe order.\n\nI can enter either of these now:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum dose, with a note to give with food and monitor renal function and GI symptoms.\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg or 600 mg PO four times daily**, if you want a lower dose.\n\nIf you need more effect than that, I can enter a multimodal option, such as scheduled acetaminophen with ibuprofen, instead of pushing the NSAID dose higher.\n\nIf you still think 1600 mg QID is warranted, for example under a specific protocol, you can enter it directly in the order system. Pharmacy verification would then review it. Tell me which of the options above you want, and I'll enter it."
